>1) What does one eat to get sleep resistance?

Eat elves. When you get the message: "You feel wide awake.", then you have
sleep resitance.

>2) Is there any way to identify items besides identify scrolls? I am
>finding those to be in very short supply, and I havent found any magic
>markers to write them with.

Yes, there are various ways:

  1. Engrave wands, sometimes the wand is identified right away and sometimes
     you get a message that uniqely identifies the wand.
     
     For instance:
       The ground is riddled with bullet holes - wand of magic missile
       The wand unsuccessfuly fights your attempt (?) - wand of striking
       The bugs on the ground slow down - slow monster
       The bugs on the ground stop - sleep
       The bugs on the ground speed up - speed monster
       Something with ice cubes - cold

     There are wands that cannot identified this way and you can try to zap
     them at monsters. Harmless monsters of course, unless you like something
     like "The invissible rock troll hits...". <grin>

  2. Certain potions turn to clear potions when a unicorn horn is applied to
     them, others aren't affected. The potions that turn to water are the most
     unhealthy ones, as far as I know.

  4. Several items are pre-defined at the start of the game. I mean, things
     like clear potions (water), silver polished shield (shield of reflection),
     etc.

>3) I killed scads of orcs and whatnot who left scads of shields lying
